<section style="background:var(--bg-warm);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding-block:2.5rem;">
  <div class="wrapper">
    <p class="section-label">Full Programme</p>
    <h1 style="max-width:640px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">Uganda Delegation, May 2–10, 2026</h1>
    <p style="font-size:.95rem;color:var(--fg-mid);max-width:640px;">
      Thanks for your interest — here's the full day-by-day programme. Questions about specific regions or lots? <a href="/#contact">Get in touch</a> or <a href="https://calendar.notion.so/meet/lorenzstckert/h932i4pxy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">book a call</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Itinerary -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrapper">
    <p class="section-label">Programme</p>
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:.5rem;">Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <p style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--fg-light);margin-bottom:2rem;">The programme below reflects what actually happened. Deviations from the original plan are noted in italics.</p>

    <div class="itinerary">

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">2 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Arrival in Entebbe</strong>
          <p>The group arrived at Entebbe International Airport at 22:50 and transferred to accommodation nearby.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">3 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Research Labs, Mukono Region &amp; CCPAU Cupping</strong>
          <p>Tour of a national coffee research institute's clone research labs and mother gardens, then a coffee farm in the Mukono region. In the evening, a professional cupping session hosted by CCPAU presented 32 lots (R1–R32) from cooperatives across the programme — the format benchmark named explicitly by multiple participants in the post-trip survey.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">4 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>MAAIF Ministerial Visit</strong>
          <p>Meeting with the Minister of Agriculture, Animal Industry and Fisheries at MAAIF headquarters, focused on value addition and Uganda's specialty positioning, followed by a press briefing. <em>Deviation: a planned farm visit in the Kyarusozi area was dropped for time.</em></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">5 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Rwenzori Processing &amp; Queen Elizabeth NP</strong>
          <p>Morning at a primary processing station in the Rwenzori mountains region (wet processing, fermentation, raised-bed drying) — one of the region's most export-ready specialty operations. Afternoon: equator crossing at Kikolongo, Kazinga Channel boat cruise, evening game drive in Queen Elizabeth National Park.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">6 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Rwashamaire Area &amp; Ankole Organic Producers</strong>
          <p>Morning game drive, then a coffee park in the Rwashamaire area (nurseries, demonstration plots, small-scale roasting facility). <em>Deviation: a planned cattle experience was replaced by a meeting with an Ankole Organic Producers Cooperative Union (ACPCU) member</em> — insight into organic certification and smallholder economics.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">7 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Masaka Region Cooperatives</strong>
          <p><em>Deviation: a planned farm visit was replaced by a morning at a cooperative in the Masaka region</em> (affiliated with a faith-based development organisation) — clear lot segregation, transparent farmer pricing, and community benefit documentation relevant to EUDR traceability. Afternoon farm walk in the same region, then travel to Kampala.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">8 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Luwero Region · Jinja</strong>
          <p>Farm visit in the Luwero region — direct-to-consumer storytelling model plus an on-site Black Soldier Fly facility turning by-products into fertiliser and feed. Afternoon travel to Jinja.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">9 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Mount Elgon Region — High-Altitude Arabica</strong>
          <p>Transit to the Kapchorwa area on the slopes of Mount Elgon. High-altitude Arabica (SL28, Bugisu, experimental varieties) that generated the strongest enthusiasm of the trip. Afternoon: Sipi Falls.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="itin-day">
        <div class="itin-date">10 May</div>
        <div class="itin-content">
          <strong>Final Debrief &amp; MAAIF Cupping Session</strong>
          <p>Return to Kampala for a debrief and a second technical cupping, hosted by MAAIF at the Uganda Coffee Development Authority lab, Lugogo. Transfer to Entebbe Airport in the evening.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Coffee Highlights -->
<section class="section section-bg">
  <div class="wrapper">
    <p class="section-label">Coffee Highlights</p>
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Three regions stood out as the strongest commercial reference points</h2>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:1.25rem;">
      <div class="step">
        <h3 style="margin-bottom:.35rem;">Rwenzori — Wet &amp; Natural Processing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:var(--fg-mid);margin:0;">One of the most export-ready specialty operations encountered, sourcing from smallholders on the mid- and upper slopes (1,400–1,900 m). Equipped for washed and natural processing with temperature-monitored fermentation and raised drying beds.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3 style="margin-bottom:.35rem;">Masaka Region — Cooperative Traceability</h3>
        <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:var(--fg-mid);margin:0;">A faith-based cooperative integrating economic inclusion for women and youth with commercial coffee production. Strong social accountability documentation and clear farmer-group traceability — directly relevant to EUDR due diligence and story-backed sourcing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3 style="margin-bottom:.35rem;">CCPAU Cupping — Lugogo</h3>
        <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:var(--fg-mid);margin:0;">The most commercially actionable station of the trip: 32 lots (R1–R32) presented with variety, region, processing, altitude, certification and available volume — a producer contact attached to every cup. Named by multiple respondents as the format benchmark for future trips.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
      <img src="/images/uganda-trip-cupping.jpg" alt="CCPAU cupping session, Lugogo, Kampala" style="width:100%;max-height:420px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:var(--radius);display:block;">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

